{"nodes": [{"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_frame", "label": "Frame 02001 - Colour Overhead Broiler House View (Siren Camera, 2022-03-01 23:01:37)", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2022-03-01T23:01:37", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Full-colour night capture under artificial house lighting. Birds are near market weight, floor coverage is close to wall-to-wall, and the litter is visibly dark and wet. The hardest frame in the chunk for instance separation because bird silhouettes merge into continuous white mass."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_high_stocking_density", "label": "High Stocking Density Late-Cycle Flock", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_file_note": null, "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In the 2022-03-01 frames the birds are near market weight and cover nearly the whole floor, so per-bird spacing approaches zero. Density is simultaneously the welfare metric of interest and the main driver of annotation and detection difficulty."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_color_daylight_mode", "label": "Colour Artificial-Light Capture Mode", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frames 02001, 02601 and 02201 (1) are captured in colour. White plumage against grey-brown litter gives strong luminance separation and the red feeder cones become an unambiguous landmark cue - a signal completely unavailable in the IR frames."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_wet_caked_litter", "label": "Wet / Caked Litter Substrate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 2022-03-01 frames show dark, glossy, compacted litter compared with the dry pale bedding of the February frames. Litter condition is itself a welfare indicator (footpad dermatitis risk) and it also shifts the background appearance distribution, which matters for any background-subtraction or colour-threshold step."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_occlusion_challenge", "label": "Bird Occlusion and Overlap Detection Challenge", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At market weight the birds physically touch and overlap, so bounding boxes have very high mutual IoU and non-maximum suppression will merge or drop true positives. This is the concrete reason a test set needs both sparse (frame02901) and saturated (frame02001, frame02601) frames: the sparse ones verify basic localisation, the saturated ones stress crowd separation."}], "edges": [{"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_frame", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_high_stocking_density", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_frame", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_color_daylight_mode", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_frame", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_wet_caked_litter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_frame", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame01701_pan_feeder_line", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_high_stocking_density", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_occlusion_challenge", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame02001.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame02001_frame", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analys